+    "findings": "<p>The handbook concerns a drinking-water monitoring program. Its method and reporting requirements do not establish category-wide food or product particle limits.</p><p>This record concerns the supplied handbook version, whose cover is dated August 9, 2022. Its introduction describes a plan to gather and report drinking-water occurrence information in a systematic way. The stated purpose is to improve information about exposure while recognizing the technical and resource demands on water systems. That purpose is narrower than declaring a product safe or setting a general particle limit for food. <a href=\"https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/drinking_water/certlic/drinkingwater/docs/2022/mp-hndbk.pdf\">Source: PDF pp. 1-3, cover and sections 1-2</a>.</p><p>In its health-effects discussion, the handbook reports that the available evidence was insufficient to develop a notification level or other numerical guidance. It identifies gaps involving effect concentrations, mechanisms and exposure from different sources. Its analytical-method discussion separately describes laboratory comparison work used to evaluate extraction and identification procedures. Method performance and a health-based interpretation are separate questions in this supplied document. <a href=\"https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/drinking_water/certlic/drinkingwater/docs/2022/mp-hndbk.pdf\">Source: PDF pp. 5-6, sections 4.2 and 4.3.1</a>.</p><p>The method comparison included spiked materials, laboratory blanks and objects that could be mistaken for plastic. The handbook also discusses training, method equivalency and contamination during sample collection. These details explain why a monitoring result depends on the implemented workflow and its controls. The supplied plan should be read with its version and intended water scope intact; its proposed implementation calendar is not presented here as a verified account of current operations. <a href=\"https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/drinking_water/certlic/drinkingwater/docs/2022/mp-hndbk.pdf\">Source: PDF pp. 6-8, sections 4.3.1-4.4</a>.</p>",
