+    "findings": "<p>The restriction applies within its substance/mixture definition and conditions, with exclusions, derogations and transition provisions. Measuring fibers released from a wipe or textile does not alone establish a violation.</p><p>The supplied instrument defines the synthetic polymer microparticles covered by its entry before describing the restriction. Its definition includes physical and compositional conditions as well as exclusions for specified polymer classes. The restriction then concerns the placing on the market of substances or mixtures in which the particles confer a sought-after characteristic. Reading the definition and operative wording together is necessary; the document is not a simple statement that every object called microplastic is prohibited. <a href=\"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/2055/oj/eng\">Source: PDF p. 11, Annex entry 78, definition and paragraph 1</a>.</p><p>The Annex distinguishes exclusions from the restriction for specified uses and circumstances, including particular contained, transformed or permanently incorporated particles. It also sets out application provisions that differ by use. These conditions are part of the supplied text and cannot be replaced by a single general claim about all plastic products. A particle released during a laboratory test does not, on its own, resolve the legal classification of a product under this entry. <a href=\"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/2055/oj/eng\">Source: PDF pp. 12-13, Annex entry 78, paragraphs 4-6</a>.</p><p>The text also contains information, disposal-instruction and reporting provisions for specified cases. Such provisions show why a description of the instrument must preserve the relevant use and conditions. This source record is a guide to the scope of the supplied version, rather than a current compliance determination for an individual licensee or product. It does not supply a health-based particle threshold for food, drinking water or human tissue. <a href=\"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/2055/oj/eng\">Source: PDF pp. 13-14, Annex entry 78, paragraphs 7-12</a>.</p>",
